Relevant columns and why they matter  

• `event_date` :  filter to ‟20180915”.  
• `event_name` :  find the event that represents a Quick‑Play completion.  
• `event_params` :  nested array that keeps the custom parameters we need.  
    – key = ‟board_type” → type of board that was played.  
    – key = ‟score” (or ‟final_score”, ‟points” …) → the player’s score.  
• `user_pseudo_id` :  (optional) lets you later de‑duplicate users / sessions if necessary.  

Typical conditions you will use  

• `event_date = '20180915'`  
• `event_name = 'quick_play_complete'`        -- (or whatever exact string you will discover)  
• `param.key = 'board_type'`  
• `param.key = 'score'` AND param.value.int_value IS NOT NULL  

